This is an interim notice, not a licensing decision. The maintainer has
chosen not to decide the licence yet, and says so here rather than
picking one for the sake of having a file.

The repository is public so that every published finding can be
audited: read it, verify it, cite it, quote it under fair dealing, and
open an issue if it is wrong. No other rights are granted at this time.

The code, the prompts, the methodology text, the story content and the
archived evidence may end up under different terms. That choice will be
revisited when there is a concrete reuse request or when the project
launches. Until then, ask: hello@yegfacts.ca.

Archived evidence files under evidence/files/ are third-party material.
Each carries its own rights status in evidence/registry/, and a file is
mirrored here only when its registry entry records that redistribution
is allowed. Nothing in this notice extends or overrides those sources'
own terms.
